---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---
<PolicyLayout title="Terms of use" description="Participation and fair-play rules for GDG Bingo community events.">
  <p>These terms apply to GDG Bingo, the community networking game operated by GDG on Campus PUP Manila organisers. By participating, you agree to follow these rules and your event organiser's published instructions.</p>
  <h2>Joining an event</h2>
  <p>Use your own Google account and an invitation provided by your organiser. An organiser may share one event invitation with all participants. Each Google account still has one participation, its own card and its own two gameplay codes. Older individual invitations remain single-use. Returning with the same account restores its saved event card. Share the event invitation only with intended participants and keep authentication details private. Event eligibility is determined by the organiser.</p>
  <h2>Playing fairly</h2>
  <p>Each participant receives two outgoing codes. Each code confirms one square once for another player. Both codes can go to the same person for different squares. You cannot claim with your own code. Codes are not tied to a specific trait: have a conversation, confirm that the person matches the selected square, then exchange a code privately.</p>
  <p>A full row, column or diagonal completes a line; the centre is free. The development default is a 12-minute round with first-line qualification and shared qualification for equal recorded first-line times. The server determines whether a claim arrived before closure. A copied code is not reserved, and an interrupted claim must be retried using the original request.</p>
  <p>Do not impersonate someone, harass participants, publish others' private information, fabricate confirmations, automate code guessing or attempt to bypass invitations, rate limits or host permissions. Organisers may restrict participation to address misuse.</p>
  <h2>Results and availability</h2>
  <p>Event organisers manage opening and closing rounds, reviewing results and communicating any prizes or eligibility requirements. Participation does not itself guarantee a prize, employment or a team placement. Self-reported or peer-confirmed skills are not certified qualifications.</p>
  <p>The service may be interrupted or changed during testing. Report a disputed or unconfirmed claim to the organiser with the event link and approximate time. Do not repeatedly create new requests or publicly post the code. A closed event cannot be restarted through the player interface.</p>
  <h2>Privacy and optional follow-up</h2>
  <p>Your display name and progress appear on the event board. Recruitment follow-up is optional and can be withdrawn without affecting gameplay. Read the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for the information collected, who can access it, retention and deletion requests. Teams conversations are separate from this website.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>For participation questions, technical problems or concerns about these terms, contact your event organiser or email <a href="mailto:gdgpup.technologydepartment@gmail.com">gdgpup.technologydepartment@gmail.com</a>. Updated terms will be published on this page.</p>
</PolicyLayout>
